{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8e671a9a-835d-4709-9b05-899e0426357a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9890cb960fa45fae","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-wjxff3vh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs in rhods-operator\n\n## Description\n\nApply the same structured log standardization to the rhods-operator's cloudmanager binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern, which already provides `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger. The remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`. This is a separate unit of work from the manager-binary conversion so it can be scheduled and released independently — whether it ships in the same release as the manager work or a subsequent one is an open product decision (PM / ODH Operator team), and this epic's scope is identical either way.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) and any shared reconciler error paths specific to the cloudmanager binary.\n- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager reconciliation error logs (kind is not implied by the shared reconciler pattern, so this is a functional requirement here, not just queryability).\n- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each of the three controllers.\n- Coordinate with the repo-wide CI lint rule delivered by the manager-binary conversion so enforcement covers cloudmanager paths once its call sites are converted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields, measured by unit test asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n- Given a cloudmanager reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs instead, measured by the repo CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n- Given the shared reconciler already emits `name`/`namespace`, when the conversion is complete, then no regression occurs in those existing fields, measured by unit test confirming both pre-existing and newly added fields are present with correct values.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: All rhods-operator (manager binary) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs — cloudmanager-binary portion.\n- P0: All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47150,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b36521ffec5564f","agent_id":"a64b12d3e6998baa7","session