{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-88328341-c5c5-4627-a604-47a4af330bc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d2e34688614b34c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-wjxff3vh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E004.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log convention\n\n## Description\n\nAuthor and publish the structured reconciliation log convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development in the rhods-operator, and publish it externally for voluntary adoption by other operator teams — specifically the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator referenced in the source RFE. Per platform policy (overlay 0008), RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies, so external adoption is voluntary and at the receiving teams' discretion; this epic's deliverable is the published specification and filed tracking issues, not adoption itself. The guideline documents the field set decided by the convention field-set investigation (required fields `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, plus any additional fields that investigation adopts), and describes the code as actually implemented.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Author a contribution guideline for new controller development specifying:\n  - The required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) and any additional fields adopted by the convention field-set decision, with the utility-vs-log-volume rationale.\n  - The camelCase naming rationale, aligning with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions.\n  - The three-problem diagnosis the change addresses: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names, and missing `resourceKind`.\n  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n  - A DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query examples for operators using Loki/CloudWatch queries that filtered on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`.\n  - Cluster-scoped resource handling (`namespace` omitted or empty).\n- Publish the convention for external operator adoption and file tracking issues in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n- Technically review the guideline against the implemented code so examples and field names match what was actually built.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the convention field-set decision, when the guideline is authored, then it specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), any adopted additional fields, the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis, measured by the published guideline containing each element.\n- Given the DSCI key migration, when the guideline is published, then it includes a migration guide with before/after query examples, measured by the migration section being present and reviewed against the implemented key names.\n- Given the code changes have landed, when the guideline is finalized, then it is technically reviewed against the implementation (examples compile/match actual log call shapes), measured by a documented technical review sign-off.\n- Given the publication deliverable, when the convention is published, then tracking issues are filed in the Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects referencing the published convention, measured by the filed issues.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The strategy's risk mitigation for external adoption delay suggests publishing the convention early; per decomposition rules the documentation epic completes after the implementation work it describes. If external adoption delay materializes, the tracking-issue filing may be pulled forward by the implementing team without changing this epic's scope.\n- External adoption by the COO team is out of this strategy's mandate (platform policy overlay 0008) and is not an acceptance criterion of this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47992,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b36521ffec5564f","agent_id":"a64b12d3e6998baa7","session_id":"affdec6a-eca1-48e8-b648-ac73c57fc806","uuid":"97dca7e6-e736-4984-8d77-2b90b2fc0b14","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:31:03.793Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 strategy"}
