{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c0af8e83914a162","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve the structured log field convention (fields beyond name, namespace,\n4\t  and resourceKind)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 0\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Resolve the structured log field convention (fields beyond name, namespace, and resourceKind)\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThe strategy's open question — owned by PM / Observability team — asks whether the structured reconciliation log convention should include fields beyond `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` (candidate examples: reconciliation attempt count, error category), trading query utility against log volume. This Investigation resolves that decision so the contribution guideline documents a final, decided field set rather than an open-ended one. It does not gate the log conversion code work: the required fields for conversion (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) are fixed by the strategy's high-level requirements and proceed regardless of this outcome.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Enumerate candidate additional structured fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) and assess the query/debugging utility each would provide for cross-controller log queries.\n35\t- Assess the log-volume impact of each candidate field across the rhods-operator's reconciliation error paths (manager and cloudmanager binaries).\n36\t- Produce a decision record specifying the final convention field set: the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) plus any adopted additional fields, with rationale for accepted and rejected candidates.\n37\t- Obtain endorsement of the decision from the PM / Observability team owners of the open question.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- Given the candidate additional fields and the utility-vs-log-volume trade-off, when the evaluation is complete, then a written decision record exists specifying the final convention field set and the rationale for each accepted/rejected candidate, measured by an endorsed decision record (PM / Observability team sign-off).\n42\t- The decision record explicitly states whether fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` are part of the convention, so the contribution guideline can be authored against it without further interpretation.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Enables the P1 requirement \"Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption\" — the decided field set is the primary content input for that guideline.\n47\t- Does not gate any P0 requirement: the conversion work's required fields are fixed by the P0 high-level requirements.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e2da5596db2197","agent_id":"a3e7f5763e29505b0","session_id":"affdec6a-eca1-48e8-b648-ac73c57fc806","uuid":"5ff58b22-3cbc-4d5f-9837-798736da3ee8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:33:02.186Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c0af8e83914a162","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
