{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb1b0dbc3b71a01d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs in rhods-operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tApply the same structured log standardization to the rhods-operator's cloudmanager binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern, which already provides `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger. The remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`. This is a separate unit of work from the manager-binary conversion so it can be scheduled and released independently — whether it ships in the same release as the manager work or a subsequent one is an open product decision (PM / ODH Operator team), and this epic's scope is identical either way.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) and any shared reconciler error paths specific to the cloudmanager binary.\n38\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n39\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager reconciliation error logs (kind is not implied by the shared reconciler pattern, so this is a functional requirement here, not just queryability).\n40\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each of the three controllers.\n41\t- Coordinate with the repo-wide CI lint rule delivered by the manager-binary conversion so enforcement covers cloudmanager paths once its call sites are converted.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields, measured by unit test asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n46\t- Given a cloudmanager reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs instead, measured by the repo CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n47\t- Given the shared reconciler already emits `name`/`namespace`, when the conversion is complete, then no regression occurs in those existing fields, measured by unit test confirming both pre-existing and newly added fields are present with correct values.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- P0: All rhods-operator (manager binary) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs — cloudmanager-binary portion.\n52\t- P0: All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e2da5596db2197","agent_id":"a3e7f5763e29505b0","session_id":"affdec6a-eca1-48e8-b648-ac73c57fc806","uuid":"50616236-fe2b-43b2-b985-beaebdc808a1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:33:03.729Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb1b0dbc3b71a01d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
