{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f261b4b14cdced6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs in rhods-operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tConvert all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, add `resourceKind` as a structured field across all controller tiers, and migrate the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from its non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the standard camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`). The manager binary covers five controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus 15 action files across four tiers: 8 component (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`). This work also delivers the CI enforcement (lint rule) and the backwards-compatibility validation for log consumers.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary (grep/static analysis), tracking coverage in a checklist — including validating the assumed ~75% figure of calls embedding resource identity.\n38\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n39\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all manager-binary controllers: service controllers, module controller (all 8 module handlers), DSC and the 8 component controllers (queryability enhancement for the latter, where kind is implied by controller name), and all 15 action files across the four tiers.\n40\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured keys from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`.\n41\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): `name` and `resourceKind` present, `namespace` omitted or empty — no spurious namespace value.\n42\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output, covering controllers, action files across all 4 tiers, and cluster-scoped resources.\n43\t- Add a CI lint rule (or static analysis check) that flags any `log.Error` call missing the required structured fields or embedding name/namespace in message text. The rule applies repo-wide (both operator binaries) — coordinate its enforcement rollout with the parallel cloudmanager-binary conversion to avoid transient CI failures.\n44\t- Backwards-compatibility validation: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack (Loki, CloudWatch) configured, trigger reconciliation errors, and verify both formats are ingested without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update any text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns.\n45\t- Document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after query examples (transition in a single release to avoid long-term inconsistency).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given a reconciliation error log call in any manager-binary controller that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs instead, measured by CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n50\t- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) instead of `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`, measured by unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to the old field names remain.\n51\t- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `resourceKind` as a structured field, measured by unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n52\t- Given an action file error log across any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields, measured by unit test asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n53\t- Given the module controller reconciles any of its 8 module handlers and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit test asserting field presence and correctness.\n54\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name` and `resourceKind`, and `namespace` is either omitted or set to empty string, measured by unit test confirming cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n55\t- Given the log format changes, when a test build is deployed to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack, then structured fields appear and log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes, and text-based alert rules relying on changed message strings are identified and updated with SRE/Support, measured by before/after log output comparison and a completed alert-rule review.\n56\t- Given the conversion is complete, when new code is contributed, then the CI lint rule flags `log.Error` calls missing the required structured fields, measured by the lint rule running in CI.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- P0: All rhods-operator (manager binary) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n61\t- P0: DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention.\n62\t- P0: All service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n63\t- P0: All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module action files).\n64\t- P0: Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n65\t- P1: DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability (bundled here — same log calls and implementation surface as the P0 conversion).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb2518830a4fe5b1","agent_id":"a2f15ca84a888e9e0","session_id":"affdec6a-eca1-48e8-b648-ac73c57fc806","uuid":"1c9b46b6-377c-43a6-8440-738e402efb5a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:39:41.505Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f261b4b14cdced6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
